        "text": "\nnatural rubber",
        "image": null
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "Dpuv8",
    "solution_text": "$$\n\\text { Nylon has amid linkage capable of forming intermolecular } \\mathrm{H} \\text {-bonding as }\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/2Z4rUd48WCf_t7lkv_gHa5HajDJtInxtryet1Vuhhl8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nDue to $\\mathrm{H}$-bonding, nylon has strong intermolecular attraction.\nCellulose is a polyhydroxy compound, also capable of forming strong intermolecular $\\mathrm{H}$-bonding. Polyvinyl chloride is a polar polymer due to carbon chlorine bond and it possess strong dipole-dipole attraction. Natural rubber is poly (isoprene), a hydrocarbon, possess weak van der Waal's attraction.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/f5i0Bw1-Ql-QNczMQa41ENvUzZ4r3kWg82G8MZwPurQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Classification of Polymers"
